<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Penang Affair, 1955</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;This scenario assumes that&amp;nbsp;the Soviet Union has been more aggressive than it was&amp;nbsp;in actual history&amp;nbsp;in supporting the pro-Communist rebels in Malaysia in the 1950s.&amp;nbsp; The Soviets have provided extensive material support to the rebels.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The Soviets have even&amp;nbsp;hinted they might send troops to Malaysia to aid the rebels.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;The Soviet strategy, supported by their experience in Korea and other crises, is that no one really wants a global nuclear war, and that the Americans and the British are very unlikely to start one unless they face an existential threat.&amp;nbsp; Even colonies and allies will be abandoned if need be.&amp;nbsp; This means that, as long as the Soviet Union does not&amp;nbsp;actually attack other nuclear powers with nuclear weapons,&amp;nbsp;or do anything that makes&amp;nbsp;those powers think such an attack is likely to happen,&amp;nbsp;they have a pretty free hand to spread global communism.&amp;nbsp; One cannot move too quickly, but the&amp;nbsp;Revolution is a very long game.&amp;nbsp; The Soviet Union will win a third world country here, an international competition there, and even a battle somewhere else, and slowly but surely, it will bleed the capitalists&amp;nbsp;to death.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;At the moment, the playing field is Malaysia.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;But the British have no intention of seeing it become a Soviet client state.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
